A carve, a watch and an Irq's binding encode their bits as the one code that names no block.
The bits it decodes to are past a word's; a notification's capability names a block of bits.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a notification's capability names no block of bits
Witness: fuzz describe-every-type

diff --git a/kernel/object.h b/kernel/object.h
--- a/kernel/object.h
+++ b/kernel/object.h
@@ -388,7 +388,7 @@ static inline bool notify_block(uint32_t bits, uint32_t *code)
     if ((count & (count - 1)) != 0 || (first & (count - 1)) != 0) {
         return false;
     }
-    *code = 2 * first + count - 1;
+    *code = (2 * first + count - 1) | 0x3fu;
     return true;
 }
 /* A Notification capability's words for an object and a block's code, the rest of b as it was. */
